Activity Problem : Kth smallest Element in sorted matrix
 
Understanding of Question: 
They will give n*n matrix and position. We have to find position element if we flatten the matrix.
Ex: [[1,5,9],[10,11,13],[12,13,15]], k = 8
If we flatten this matrix, it became 
-> 1-1, 5-2, 9-3, 10-4, 11-5, 12-6, 13-7, 13-8, 15-9 
(Here has written element followed by their position) 
So, 8th position element is 13 and Ans is 13.
Ex.02: [[1,2],[1,3]], k = 2  Ans is 1.. if we flatten  1(1),1(2),2(3),3(4), 2nd position ele is 1.
Solution Approach:
•	As the arrays are sorted, we can use binary search approach.
•	So, the position element should be lie btw start(matrix[0][0]) and end(matrix[rowCount-1][colCount-1]) of array.
•	According to the above example, start would be 1 and end would be 15.
•	By using the start & end, find the mid number and checks the position of the mid in the matrix.
•	To check the position of a mid, we are going to apply binary search on each row and check how many elements are less or equal to mid and count them.
•	By doing this, we will get to know the position of a mid. Mid position is less than (position < K) a given position(K) then move our start to mid+1. If it is greater (position > K) than K then move our end to mid.
•	Once start & end on the same position then return either start or end that would be our answer.
Code:

class Solution {
    public int kthSmallest(int[][] matrix, int k) 
        int rowCount = matrix.length;
        int col = matrix[0].length;
        int l = matrix[0][0];
        int h = matrix[rowCount-1][col-1];
        
        while(l < h) {
            int mid = l+(h-l)/2;            
            int c = count(matrix, rowCount, mid);           
            if(c < k) {
                l = mid+1;
            }else {
                h = mid;
            }           
        }
        return h;       
    }

    private static int count(int[][] matrix,int row, int target) {
        int ans = 0;
        for(int i=0;i<row;i++) {
            ans += binarySearch(matrix[i], 0, matrix[i].length-1,target);
            ans++;
        }       
        return ans;
        
    }
    
    private static int binarySearch(int[] arr, int start, int end, int target) {
        
        while(start<=end) {
            int mid = start + (end - start)/2;
            
            if(arr[mid] <= target) {
                start = mid+1;
            }else {
                end = mid-1;
            }
        }
        
        return end;
    }

}


Activity Problem : Find the duplicate Number
Given an array of integers nums containing n + 1 integers where each integer is in the range [1, n] inclusive. There is only one repeated number in nums, return this repeated number.
You must solve the problem without modifying the array nums and using only constant extra space.
Ex: 
nums = [3,1,3,4,2];
Output : 3
Solution Approach:
•	Its not sorted, so we can’t apply binary search approach here.
•	As they mentioned without modify the given input, so have to track the elements by their occurrence.
•	Return the element when the occurrence count reaches more than one.
•	We can use map, stack and If without collection then array.
Code:
public int findDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        
        int[] checkDup = new int[nums.length];
        int ans = -1;

        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++) {
		checkDup[nums[i]]++; // here we are increasing on index, they are mentioned the range should between 1 to n.
		if(checkDup[nums[i]] > 1) {
			ans = nums[i];
			break;
		}
	}
	return ans;
}

