Decode String:
Question: Given an encoded string, return its decoded string.
The encoding rule is: k[encoded_string], where the encoded_string inside the square brackets is being repeated exactly k times. Note that k is guaranteed to be a positive integer.
I/P: 2[abc]3[cd]ef
O/P: abcabccdcdcdef 
Solution Approach:
•	By using stack, will decode string from starting of the string until ‘]’. 
o	For ex. 2[abc] , insert these to stack until ]. Once we found the ] then will take the alpahabets abc – this loop will run till [ . 
o	Once found [ then we focus on the number part.
o	Once number(n) and alphabet string found then, loop the alphabet for n times.
o	Then add the repeated string to stack again.
Code:
public String decodeString(String s) {
        Stack<String> stack = new Stack<>();
        for(char ch : s.toCharArray()){
            if(ch!=']'){
                stack.push(String.valueOf(ch));
            }else{
                StringBuffer str = new StringBuffer();
                while(!stack.peek().equals("[")){
                    str.insert(0,stack.pop());
                }
                stack.pop();//Removing [
                StringBuffer num = new StringBuffer();
                while(!stack.isEmpty() && Character.isDigit(stack.peek().charAt(0))){
                    num.insert(0,stack.pop());
                } 
                String repeating = str.toString().repeat(Integer.parseInt(num.toString()));
                stack.push(repeating);
            }
        }

        StringBuffer ans = new StringBuffer();
        for(String str: stack) ans.append(str);

        return ans.toString();
    }

