Min Stack
Design a stack that supports push, pop, top, and retrieving the minimum element in constant time.
Implement the MinStack class:
•	MinStack() initializes the stack object.
•	void push(int value) pushes the element value onto the stack.
•	void pop() removes the element on the top of the stack.
•	int top() gets the top element of the stack.
•	int getMin() retrieves the minimum element in the stack.
You must implement a solution with O(1) time complexity for each function.
Solution Approach:
•	In stack pop(), push(), top() all these actions will take only O(1) time complexity.
•	Have to maintain another minStack to get O(1) on getMin() actions. 
•	In the minStack() we’ll maintain only lower values.
Code:
class MinStack {

    Stack<Integer> stack;
    Stack<Integer> minStack;

    public MinStack() {
        stack = new Stack<>();
        minStack = new Stack<>();
    }
    
    public void push(int value) {

        if(stack.isEmpty()){
            minStack.push(value);
        }else{
            if(minStack.peek() > value){
                minStack.push(value);
            }else{
                minStack.push(minStack.peek());
            }
        }

        stack.push(value);
        
    }
    
    public void pop() {
        stack.pop();
        minStack.pop();
    }
    
    public int top() {
        return stack.peek();
    }
    
    public int getMin() {
        return minStack.peek();
    }
}



