Largest Rectangle in Histogram
Given an array of heights, consider width of each height bar is 1. Calculate and return the max area of rectangle.
Solution Approach:
 	•	To frame a rectangle, first we have to find NSE and PSE
•	NSE – Next Small Element
•	PSE – Previous Small Element
•	NSE points used to know, how far we can extend our height, that’s why we checking the next small element of current element.
•	Same as PSE used to know from where we can calculate the width.
•	Once found NSE and PSE for current element, by calculate NSE – PSE, will get the width, after that we can multiple our current height with width will get the rectangle area.


Code:
int[] arr = {2,1,5,6,2,3};
		int maxWidth = 0;
		int n = arr.length;
		Stack<Integer> stack = new Stack<>();
		int[] nse = new int[n];
		int[] pse = new int[n];
		
		//to find nse - next small element
		for(int i = n-1;i>=0;i--) {
			while(!stack.isEmpty() && arr[i] <= arr[stack.peek()]) {
				stack.pop();
			}
			
			nse[i] = stack.isEmpty()?n-1:stack.peek();
			stack.push(i);
		}
		
		stack.clear();
		
		//to find pse - previous small element
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {
			while(!stack.isEmpty() && arr[i] <= arr[stack.peek()]) {
				stack.pop();
			}
			
			pse[i] = stack.isEmpty() ? 0:stack.peek();
			stack.push(i);
		}
		
		for(int i=0;i<n;i++) {
			int area = arr[i] * (nse[i] - pse[i] - 1); // why -1? For NSE, we are setting N for no small element found and in PSE setting -1 for no small element in previous. So compromise this, we are using -1.
			maxWidth = Math.max(maxWidth, area);
		}
		
		System.out.println("Max Width : "+maxWidth);
		System.out.println("Next Small Element "+Arrays.toString(nse));
		System.out.println("Previous Small Element "+Arrays.toString(pse));
		

